<section id="engine" data-transition="fade" style="background:#F7F6F2;color:#14213D;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:88px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px">
<div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px">
<p style="font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#B5531C;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase">The engine problem</p>
<h2 style="font-size:60px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.1">One token through a 35B MoE on an 8 GB Jetson</h2>
<p style="font-size:28px;color:#4A5568">Qwen3.6-35B-A3B: 40 layers × 256 experts, 8 chosen per layer per token. Experts are 18.3 GiB of a 20.8 GiB file; the machine has 7.4 GiB of shared memory.</p>
</div>
<div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px;background:#FFFFFF;border:1px solid #E1DED6;border-radius:16px;padding:28px 32px">
<p style="font-size:26px;font-weight:600;color:#4A5568">Stock llama.cpp cf34d311 · <span style="color:#14213D">-ngl 99 -cmoe -lm mmap</span> (configuration)</p>
<div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:16px">
<div style="flex:1;background:#E8EEF6;border-radius:12px;padding:20px"><p style="font-size:26px;line-height:1.3"><b>GPU</b>: attention and router for layer L (2.5 GiB, resident)</p></div>
<x-connector style="width:48px;color:#14213D"></x-connector>
<div style="flex:1;background:#E8EEF6;border-radius:12px;padding:20px"><p style="font-size:26px;line-height:1.3">Router picks 8 experts: about 15 MiB of weights for this layer</p></div>
<x-connector style="width:48px;color:#14213D"></x-connector>
<div style="flex:1.2;background:#FBE3D3;border:2px solid #B5531C;border-radius:12px;padding:20px"><p style="font-size:26px;line-height:1.3"><b>CPU</b> expert matmul touches mmap’d pages. Not resident → page fault → compute thread waits on NVMe</p></div>
</div>
</div>
<div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px;background:#FFFFFF;border:1px solid #E1DED6;border-radius:16px;padding:28px 32px">
<p style="font-size:26px;font-weight:600;color:#4A5568">With expert streaming (software: patches to llama.cpp; switches set by env)</p>
<div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:16px">
<div style="flex:1;background:#E3EDE6;border-radius:12px;padding:20px"><p style="font-size:26px;line-height:1.3"><b>Hook</b> before layer L’s expert matmul sees the router’s choice</p></div>
<x-connector style="width:48px;color:#14213D"></x-connector>
<div style="flex:1;background:#E3EDE6;border-radius:12px;padding:20px"><p style="font-size:26px;line-height:1.3"><b>Demand fill</b>: 16 workers read only the missing ranges</p></div>
<x-connector style="width:48px;color:#14213D"></x-connector>
<div style="flex:1;background:#E3EDE6;border-radius:12px;padding:20px"><p style="font-size:26px;line-height:1.3"><b>Predictive read</b>: guess L+1’s experts, read while L computes</p></div>
<x-connector style="width:48px;color:#14213D"></x-connector>
<div style="flex:0.9;background:#E8EEF6;border-radius:12px;padding:20px"><p style="font-size:26px;line-height:1.3">Same matmul finds the weights in memory</p></div>
</div>
</div>
<div style="display:flex;gap:24px">
<p style="flex:1;font-size:24px;line-height:1.35;color:#14213D"><b>Unchanged:</b> weights, math, router choice, sampling. Wrong guess = wasted read; late read = demand reads the rest.</p>
