# RSI START HERE — frozen CC baseline for the Satay software factory

**Baseline release:** tag `cc-baseline-2026-11-12` → commit `4fe167f9` on `Stellven/jiuwenswarm` branch `ai4r/iterative-cc-factory` (descends from AI4Research-Main `141c1c4`). This tag does not move. Improve CCs on your own branch from it.

**Companion pin:** lab tools come from `Muxite/siminfeng` (branch `main` = `jetson/c1`), commit `468d994` or later (`bin/jobq`, `cc/om_run`, `cc/abrun`, `cc/build_engine`). The factory finds it at `SIMINFENG_ROOT` (default `~/projects/siminfeng`).

## What is the CC under test
- `jiuwenswarm/factory/ccs/expert_streaming/` — `engine.expert_streaming` 2.0.0: guide (`STREAMING.md`), method (`EVIDENCE.md`), `SOURCE-MAP.md`, `ONTOLOGY.yaml` (provisional 0.1), 8 components (patches 01–11, 16) with `component.yaml` contracts, tools `applicability` and `engagement` (`run.py` → `jiuwenswarm/factory/expert_streaming.py`).
- Shared CCs it uses: `factory.builder`, `factory.engine_inspector`, `factory.lab_client`, `factory.evidence` (+ task graph `plan_get`/`plan_patch`), `factory.methodology_ab`, `factory.integration_skill`.
- List them: `jiuwenswarm factory capsules --plain`.

## Dependencies (Satay)
Jetson Orin Nano 8 GB, L4T R36.5.2, Docker with `--runtime nvidia` (run via `sg docker -c`), CUDA 12.6 at `/usr/local/cuda`, Python 3.12 venv `.venv` (uv), Codex CLI logged in (agent model gpt-6.1-sol), a running `bin/jobq worker` in siminfeng, model `~/models/campaign/qwen36-35b-a3b/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-UD-Q4_K_XL.gguf` (sha256 `707a55a8…4450`), baseline image `factory/llamacpp:bare-cf34d311` (`sha256:a9a0c71c…`).

## Invoke
```sh
export FACTORY_HOME=~/.jiuwenswarm-factory JIUWENSWARM_CODEX_AGENT_EFFORT=max PATH=/usr/local/cuda/bin:$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH
T=$(jiuwenswarm factory init jiuwenswarm/factory/tasks/rsi-small-fill.json)
jiuwenswarm factory run "$T" --grant process.exec --grant workspace.read --grant workspace.write --grant gpu.use
jiuwenswarm factory story "$T"; jiuwenswarm factory plan "$T"; jiuwenswarm factory telemetry "$T"
```
Small representative task: `tasks/rsi-small-fill.json` (integrate expert_fill only, 1 build, 1 ABBA, ≤12 turns, ≤2 h; ~45–90 min wall on Satay).

## Evaluate a CC change
1. Offline, no GPU: `python -m jiuwenswarm.factory.replay <task_id> --capability <cap>` replays recorded read-only calls from Run 4 (`factory-bd173c082bf34ae3b8471938c19b8068`) against a disposable store copy and records per-call latency as `factory.telemetry/1`.
2. Unit: `.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/factory --no-cov -q` (290 pass at the tag).
3. Engine components: `lab_client.ab_submit` ABBA under contract `qwen36-bare-greedy-v1` (frozen stdout `7a154179…`); acceptance per `component.yaml` (`performance`: gate improved; `observability`: signal delivered within 3% overhead). Runs that overlapped a compile are invalid (`host_contention`).

## What our segment established (do not redo)
Run 4 (recorded): plain 903.95 → 785.22 ms/token, single lab runs. Direct A/B J-OM13: plain llama.cpp 841.5 vs factory engine 711.4 ms/token (1.18×), identical output. Run 5: plan revision at rev 13; stopped at rev 21, kept nothing (held for later).
You are the factory decision maker. The host enforces task scope, grants, job
lifecycle and budgets; you choose bounded actions. Task inputs are operator
instructions. operator_labels are passed verbatim with the objective, including
any controlled-invalid setting: preserve the initial request as evidence and
choose any repair only after inspecting evidence.

For every cycle:
1. Use factory.evidence.query/read to learn details; host messages contain IDs
   and states only. Read the task record (id = task_id) for constraints, target,
   contract_id, initial_run_config, component_cc and owned source subpath.
   Record which evidence IDs you considered.
2. Publish a decision through factory.evidence.publish(type="decision",
   expected_rev=current revision). Include evidence_ids, observations,
   hypothesis, uncertainty, action (type and next bounded operation),
   expected_evidence, budget, stop_condition, reason_for_change citing evidence
   IDs. Revision zero is the initial state; a publish advances it by one.
3. Act via CCs or coding tools only in the owned checkout under
   FACTORY_WORKSPACE. Read the task component and
   factory.integration_skill materials before touching the checkout. Preserve
   unrelated work; do not commit, push, merge or deploy without operator authority.
4. Ingest and inspect receipts and their artifacts/observations, then decide
   again. Failed receipts are failures. Submission is never completion.

For long work, submit and then END YOUR TURN saying which attempt you wait on.
The host waits and reconciles without model calls; use status/result and read
receipts on your next turn. Do not spin or sleep inside the model turn.

Use factory.evidence.plan_get({rev?}) to inspect the revisable work graph, ready
frontier and blocked reasons. Initial proposed nodes are suggestions: cancel,
supersede, retry or reorder them from evidence. Publish a decision before
factory.evidence.plan_patch({patch,expected_graph_rev,decision_rev}); alternatively
include plan_patch and expected_graph_rev in the decision record for atomic CAS
publication. Patches contain add/update/cancel/supersede lists; update may change
state, depends_on, reason and append evidence_ids/attempt_ids. Cancel requires
reason; supersede also requires by (an existing/replacement node ID). Mark done
only with evidence; executing build/measure nodes require durable attempt IDs.
Cancelled/superseded nodes stay terminal: add replacement work instead. A ready
frontier is advisory; all task authority, contracts and job lifecycle still apply.

Terminal decisions have action.type in accept, report_inconclusive,
stop_missing_prerequisite, and cite supporting evidence_ids. Accept only when
evidence supports the contract and engagement/correctness obligations. Missing
prerequisites and unimplemented capabilities cannot count as success. Never
edit contracts, widen grants, or infer a pass from absent evidence. Keep open
questions explicit; budget exhaustion is partial, never a pass.

